 ## Overview
-This method aggregates complementary geometric and appearance information from multiple camera views to enhance the radiance field representation of dynamic humans [S1, unofficial]. It combines time-augmented skeletal features, which provide robust geometric priors via a SMPL model, with pixel-aligned image features, which capture high-frequency visual details [S1, unofficial]. By using a cross-attention mechanism to weigh these features based on their compatibility, the method resolves ambiguities in single-view observations and improves rendering quality for articulated subjects [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard NeRF by explicitly integrating skeletal priors and multi-view consistency through attention, rather than relying solely on positional encoding of raw coordinates [S1, unofficial].
+This method integrates geometric priors from a parametric human model (SMPL) with multi-view image features to improve the quality of neural radiance fields for human performance rendering [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of ambiguous geometry and texture in single-view or poorly constrained multi-view setups by using skeletal features as a robust, time-augmented geometric backbone [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard NeRF which relies solely on positional encoding of 3D coordinates, this approach explicitly retrieves features from a learned skeletal volume and aggregates them with pixel-aligned image features using a cross-attention mechanism [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [SUDS](14964-suds.md) by using a parametric model prior rather than unsupervised depth, and from [Rip-NeRF](15532-rip-nerf.md) by focusing on articulated human performance rather than static geometry [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Inputs:** A 3D query point $x \in \mathbb{R}^3$ in world space; a set of $C$ input images $I_{c,t}$ at time $t$; camera parameters for each view; a SMPL model instance at time $t$; and the viewing direction $d \in \mathbb{R}^3$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Outputs:** Volume density $\tilde{\sigma}_t(x)$ and RGB color $\tilde{r}^g_{bt}(x)$ for the query point [S1, unofficial].
+The method processes a query 3D point $\mathbf{x}$ and a viewing direction $\mathbf{d}$ at a specific time $t$ across $C$ camera views. It retrieves skeletal and image features, aggregates them via attention, and predicts density and color.
 
-**Data Structures:**
-*   **Skeletal Features ($s^0_{c,t}$):** A $d$-dimensional feature vector retrieved at the query location via trilinear interpolation within a SparseConvNet representation of the SMPL volume [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Pixel-aligned Features ($p^x_{c,t}$):** A $d$-dimensional feature vector extracted from image $I_{c,t}$ at the 2D projection of $x$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Attention Weights ($mv\_att^x$):** A $C \times C$ matrix representing cross-view compatibility scores [S1, unofficial].
+**Inputs and Outputs**
+*   **Inputs:** Query point $\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^3$, viewing direction $\mathbf{d} \in \mathbb{R}^3$, time $t$, camera poses for $C$ views.
+*   **Outputs:** Volume density $\tilde{\sigma}_t(\mathbf{x})$ and RGB color $\tilde{r}^g_{bt}(\mathbf{x})$.
 
